    "id": 20393895,
    "status": "Open",
    "summary": "Stormwater Drainage / Drenaje de Aguas Pluviales",
    "description": "This is a second request to clear a drainage area down Jewell Street between Ridge and Union.  North/East side.  The DPW solved an ongoing problem by clearing the the first time about 4 years ago.  Unfortunately it needs cleaning out each year.\n\nThere are no houses on this side of Jewell.- but across from several.\n\nIt was dug out by DPW a few years ago and has allowed heavy rain water to flow downhill to a street drain near Union St.   Thank you!\n\nIt keeps the water from crossing the street and running down driveways on the South/West side.  This takes it into the properties downhill on Union St.\n\nUnfortunately it's currently filled with vegetation - leaves, etc. which is blocking the gutter.  With the rain coming this week, I'm concerned and requesting that DPW remove the debris that will block the flow to the drain.",
