  {
    "id": 20393859,
    "status": "Open",
    "summary": "Pothole/Road Condition / Bache (hoyo)/Condici\u00f3n de Carreteras",
    "description": "The manhole cover in the street in front of 292 Knight Drive in San Rafael looks like it was first popped up by the heavy machinery that has been working on this street daily since July or so. Then this manhole cover had been broken into two or more pieces, likely by the same type of machinery. It was then covered with sand and has two orange cones on each side. This sits right in the middle of our narrow street, which means that cars must drive around, which is potentially dangerous. This should be fixed as soon as possible. Also, you'll notice that the house at 292 Knight Drive has two large piles of stones against the curb and extending well into the street, with orange cones around the piles. These piles of stones have been there for at least 4 months. The homeowner seems to be totally disregarding the fact that these piles of stones make cars have to veer away from the piles coming up the street. The situation is made considerably worse by the broken manhole cover that is only a few feet away from those piles. Again, this combination is creating a dangerous obstruction in the middle of Upper Knight Drive. ",
